Not quite a CD for learning lojban, but if you want to hear it being
spoken and learn a bit:
http://www.nemorathwald.com/jbocradi/jbocradi.html

I saw somewhere that someone is developing content for a tape on
learning lojban..but I don't know how far along that is

For interactive software, there's Parallel 2
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Parallel+2&bl

or any on the list here:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Software+assisted+learning&bl
or the games in the lojbanic software section of the lojban.org site.

